The attached image displays immunofluorescence microscopy of skeletal muscle 24 hours post-injection, showing the local inflammatory response and cellular uptake of AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) with ovalbumin (OVA). The top row illustrates the Nano-11+OVA injection site, revealing infiltration of Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages (green, first panel), MHCII+ cells (green, second panel), and 1A8+ neutrophils (green, third panel), with Mac-2+ and MHCII+ cells showing intracellular Nano-11. The fourth panel highlights F4/80+ macrophages. The bottom row serves as a control (soluble OVA only), demonstrating negligible inflammatory cell recruitment. This confirms Nano-11's ability to induce a transient inflammatory response at the injection site, facilitating the recruitment and antigen uptake by various immune cells, particularly monocytes and MHCII+ cells.